{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfia3D8RoF2pvj84oF61q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan phase is done. I wrote `journal/2026-10-04/20-brief.md` and set `pack`, `slug`, `title` and `plan: \"done\"` in `state.json`. I didn't build or render anything, so the arithmetic and layout in the brief are untested.\n\n**`model.selfDeclared`:** `run.json` already held `claude-sonnet-5-5` when I read it, which matches what I believe I am. I didn't rewrite it, so I can't confirm that I wrote it myself.\n\n**The pick:** `@one-a-day/sports/cubing-average-card/v1`, titled \"Cubing Average Card\". It's a still image at 1080x1080, in the existing `sports` pack, so no new pack.\n\n**What the card shows:**\n- **Average:** the user gives 3, 5 or 12 solves, and the card works out Mo3, Ao5 or Ao12 from the count.\n- **Bars:** one bar per solve. Dropped best and worst solves are in parentheses with a hollow bar. DNF rows get no bar.\n- **Headline:** the average, with a `NEW PB` chip and a delta against `previousPb`. A slower average is shown with a plus sign and no red.\n- **Layout:** two columns for 16:9 canvases, stacked for square and portrait.\n\n**Props:** ten, mostly optional. The shipped defaults will be the winning variant's.\n\n**Test vectors:** I worked four cases by hand for the build to pin.\n- The defaults give `27.80`, which is `-0.55` against a `28.35` PB.\n- An Ao12 case lands on 2834.5 hundredths, so integer rounding gives `28.35` where a float could give `28.34`.\n- A Mo3 case gives `19.18`, and a Mo3 with a DNF gives `DNF`.\n- An Ao5 with two DNFs gives a `DNF` average.\n\n**Variants:** three, each one idea different. All three share one `bar` prop and one `avgLine` prop.\n- **a:** bars drawn from zero.\n- **b:** the same bars plus an average tick in every track.\n- **c:** bars showing distance from the average.\n\n**Day 13 lesson:** that day's NO SHIP was for bars missing from the render, so the rubric now requires the stills themselves to show one bar per non-DNF solve.\n\n**Weak spots, written into the brief:**\n- Timer apps already draw their own share cards.\n- The template doesn't parse the csTimer block.\n- Ao50 and Ao100 are refused.\n- The WCA's whole-second rounding for times over ten minutes isn't handled.\n- Bars drawn from zero look alike at the defaults."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":73330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878},"output_tokens":811,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a55a0a7a-83c2-415b-a1d7-0cdfd89c384d","uuid":"cf1b5123-00d3-4fec-8141-078f1a63123f","timestamp":"2026-10-05T05:53:06.477Z","request_id":"req_011Cfia3Cqp6QeeHGUMrQo1L"}
